        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>The Black Bananas singer knows all the words to Rapper’s Delight and relates to AC/DC, but which song reminds her of a heartbreaking theft?</p><p><strong>The first song I fell in love with</strong><br> Van Halen’s Runnin’ With the Devil. I was five or six and I went to visit my cousin Tommy who was much older. He was on a hockey team and we went to see them practise before the game and they had Runnin’ With the Devil on really loud. I was like: “Wait, what’s this?!”</p><p><strong>The song I do at karaoke<br></strong>You Shook Me All Night Long by AC/DC. Me and Brian Johnson – my voice has that thing, you know?</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/aug/30/jennifer-herrema-honest-playlist-sugarhill-gang-van-halen-lou-reed-acdc\">Continue reading...</a>"
